This directory is not read by openRuyi's system trust module.
The active input directories are /etc/pki/trust and /usr/share/pki/trust.
Existing files are kept. They are not imported automatically: importing a
previously ignored certificate can change system trust.

Before migration, back up both the old and active input directories.
Review each certificate's identity, fingerprint and intended trust settings.
For local policy, copy each approved file into /etc/pki/trust, keeping its
relative location: anchors/ for trusted CAs, blocklist/ for distrusted CAs,
and the root directory for files with embedded trust settings.
Do not put a blocklisted certificate into anchors/.

If the destination exists, compare the contents. Do not overwrite different
contents. Resolve conflicting trust settings before importing either file.
For files owned by an RPM, correct that package rather than moving its files.

Run update-ca-trust, then verify both the expected trust and distrust with
the affected applications. Remove the old copy only after verification.
To undo a migration, restore the active inputs from the backup and run
update-ca-trust again.
